I sing the while.

27
00:11:33,183 --> 00:11:35,166
Sweet joy befall thee.

28
00:11:39,583 --> 00:11:47,875
For Bhante, to thank you for setting the wheel of the Dharma in motion at Satipaña, here is your local group's illustration of the Four Noble Truths.

29
00:11:51,301 --> 00:12:01,395
First Noble Truth The world is afflicted by death and decay, but the wise do not grieve, having realized the nature of the world.

30
00:12:05,201 --> 00:12:06,604
Second Noble Truth

31
00:12:07,528 --> 00:12:14,015
Whoever is overcome by this wretched craving, his sorrows grow like grass after rain.

32
00:12:14,976 --> 00:12:22,024
But whoever overcomes this wretched craving, his sorrows fall away like water from a lotus leaf.

33
00:12:24,986 --> 00:12:27,950
Third noble truth, there is an end to suffering.

34
00:12:29,471 --> 00:12:33,335
There is an island, an island which you cannot go beyond.

35
00:12:34,076 --> 00:12:36,337
It is a place of nothingness,

36
00:12:36,436 --> 00:12:39,057
of non-possession and non-attachment.

37
00:12:39,639 --> 00:12:45,904
It is the total end of death and decay, and this is why I call it nibbana.

38
00:12:49,048 --> 00:12:52,971
Fourth noble truth, there is a path to the end of suffering.

39
00:12:54,592 --> 00:12:56,575
No one saves us but ourselves.

40
00:12:57,475 --> 00:12:59,356
No one can and no one may.

41
00:13:00,418 --> 00:13:03,321
We ourselves must walk the path.

42
00:13:06,034 --> 00:13:12,121
The following cards represent the Noble Eightfold Path.

43
00:13:15,365 --> 00:13:26,759
With the entire cessation of this ignorance, intentional activities cease.

44
00:13:28,715 --> 00:13:41,472
Thus does the cessation of this entire aggregation of suffering result.

45
00:13:44,697 --> 00:13:47,400
O Master, is it proper for a monk to use email?

46
00:13:48,601 --> 00:13:50,804
Sure, as long as there are no attachments.

47
00:13:53,788 --> 00:13:56,393
I said to the wanting creature inside me,

48
00:13:57,182 --> 00:13:59,044
What is this river you want to cross?

49
00:13:59,865 --> 00:14:02,990
There are no travellers on the river road, and no road.

50
00:14:03,629 --> 00:14:06,693
Do you see anyone moving about on that bank, or nesting?

51
00:14:08,235 --> 00:14:11,720
There is no river at all, and no boat, and no boatman.

52
00:14:12,541 --> 00:14:15,443
There is no tow-rope either, and no one to pull it.

53
00:14:16,284 --> 00:14:24,894
There is no ground, no sky, no time, no bank, no ford, and there is no body, and no mind.

54
00:14:26,292 --> 00:14:30,296
Do you believe that there is some place that will make the soul less thirsty?

55
00:14:31,658 --> 00:14:33,539
In that great absence you will find nothing.

56
00:14:34,821 --> 00:14:37,945
Be strong then and enter into your own body.

57
00:14:38,946 --> 00:14:41,008
There you have a solid place for your feet.

58
00:14:41,989 --> 00:14:43,171
Think about it carefully.

59
00:14:43,971 --> 00:14:45,212
Don't go off somewhere else.

60
00:14:46,673 --> 00:14:54,442
Kabir says this, just throw away all thoughts of imaginary things and stand firm in that which you are.

61
00:14:57,645 --> 00:15:03,697
For your 70th birthday Bhante, we thought we would update a verse from the Parinibbana Sutta.

62
00:15:07,524 --> 00:15:10,971
Come Ananda, let us go to the Satipanya shrine.

63
00:15:11,712 --> 00:15:14,658
Beautiful Ananda is the Satipanya shrine.

64
00:15:17,102 --> 00:15:37,591
for hire messrs maurice mole and sons purveyors of quality unwanted holes full dissatisfaction guaranteed or your money back no lawn too small to ruin for a reminder of impermanence you could not find better that's why all little moles should be wished matter

65
00:15:39,783 --> 00:15:49,176
This is a card based on the Wheel of Dependent Origination from the Insight Meditation Group of Dublin, with apologies to dandelion lovers everywhere.

66
00:15:52,360 --> 00:15:53,402
Have mercy, bounty.

67
00:15:53,682 --> 00:15:54,823
Don't cut off my head.

68
00:15:55,424 --> 00:15:56,986
Listen to my tale of woe.

69
00:15:57,548 --> 00:16:00,913
It's called The Wheel of Dandelion Origination.

70
00:16:04,256 --> 00:16:05,418
Avijja.

71
00:16:06,900 --> 00:16:08,323
I never meant any harm.

72
00:16:09,085 --> 00:16:10,508
I don't know how it started.

73
00:16:11,028 --> 00:16:12,030
It was like a whirlwind.

74
00:16:12,532 --> 00:16:14,296
Everything was going round and round.

75
00:16:15,077 --> 00:16:16,039
Nothing made sense.

76
00:16:18,423 --> 00:16:25,077
Avijja, ignorance, is a condition for Sankara.

77
00:16:26,442 --> 00:16:30,208
Whirling in the torrent, there was a seed, a seed of willpower.

78
00:16:30,970 --> 00:16:36,080
What I had previously desired and built my life around was written into that tiny seed.

79
00:16:36,780 --> 00:16:37,863
It could all happen again.

80
00:16:37,903 --> 00:16:39,024
Yippee!

81
00:16:40,246 --> 00:16:44,534
Sankara, habitual formations, are a condition for...

82
00:16:47,687 --> 00:16:51,873
Now, where to plant that seed?

83
00:16:52,572 --> 00:16:55,437
Ah yes, the ground of discriminative consciousness.

84
00:16:56,738 --> 00:17:04,666
Where the seed was known as separate with a past and a future, in that rich soil a seed could settle and flourish.

85
00:17:06,209 --> 00:17:13,576
Vijnana, consciousness, is a condition for nama-rupa.

86
00:17:15,176 --> 00:17:19,983
No sooner had the seed settled than it began to germinate, dividing in two.

87
00:17:20,785 --> 00:17:25,332
One part attracted to the earth to be rooted, physical, grounded.

88
00:17:26,252 --> 00:17:30,338
The other attracted to the skies to explore the world, make contact.

89
00:17:31,942 --> 00:17:42,517
Nama-rupa, mentality, materiality, is a condition for salayatana.

90
00:17:42,537 --> 00:17:44,559
Six channels opened up.

91
00:17:44,894 --> 00:17:46,777
Six doorways to the outer world.

92
00:17:47,598 --> 00:17:54,349
Now the internal world was ready and waiting for some external stimulus to open one channel.

93
00:17:55,471 --> 00:17:59,138
Salayatana, six sense spaces, are a condition for.

94
00:18:02,144 --> 00:18:02,585
Pasa.

95
00:18:04,327 --> 00:18:07,092
A ray of sunlight opened up the doorway of the eye.

96
00:18:07,894 --> 00:18:10,377
Immediately the seedling burst through.

97
00:18:11,994 --> 00:18:15,458
Now its inner world was in contact with the outer world.

98
00:18:16,318 --> 00:18:19,300
Passer, contact, is a condition for.

99
00:18:22,104 --> 00:18:22,624
Wegener.

100
00:18:23,865 --> 00:18:28,489
The sunshine was so pleasant, lovely, nourishing, gorgeous.

101
00:18:29,049 --> 00:18:31,090
The stem grew leaves to soak it up.

102
00:18:31,872 --> 00:18:34,114
Maybe it would have been better to leave it at that.

103
00:18:35,836 --> 00:18:38,458
Just basking in the sunshine while it lasted.

104
00:18:39,218 --> 00:18:41,039
But then the trouble started.

105
00:18:42,336 --> 00:18:49,548
Vedana, feeling, is a condition for tanha.

106
00:18:49,567 --> 00:18:51,529
Something deep down demanded more.

107
00:18:52,592 --> 00:18:55,596
More of the sunshine, more of the lovely stuff.

108
00:18:56,958 --> 00:18:59,923
It was like thirst, it just had to be satisfied.

109
00:19:00,323 --> 00:19:07,894
With a great surge of energy, a big stem started to shoot upwards, demanding more, more, more.

110
00:19:07,933 --> 00:19:11,819
Tanha, desire, is a condition for

111
00:19:14,550 --> 00:19:15,332
Upadana.

112
00:19:16,515 --> 00:19:17,676
Then I blossomed.

113
00:19:17,957 --> 00:19:19,840
I had found myself at last.

114
00:19:20,701 --> 00:19:25,330
Aren't I beautiful, marvellous, golden and gorgeous like the sun itself?

115
00:19:26,692 --> 00:19:29,337
Now all I had to do was hold on tight.

116
00:19:31,781 --> 00:19:32,443
Upadana.

117
00:19:32,864 --> 00:19:34,887
Clinging is a condition for...

118
00:19:37,483 --> 00:19:38,164
Bhāva.

119
00:19:39,047 --> 00:19:56,184
Till, by sheer willpower, I put forth all these seeds to give the world more of me, millions and millions more, and so Bhāva becoming is a condition for Jāti.

120
00:19:58,122 --> 00:20:01,547
Behold ye, the dandelion dynasty has been born.

121
00:20:02,328 --> 00:20:04,491
This poor old stupor hasn't a chance.

122
00:20:04,913 --> 00:20:05,532
Purify?

123
00:20:05,574 --> 00:20:06,535
No way.

124
00:20:06,976 --> 00:20:08,218
Let's dandify.

125
00:20:10,381 --> 00:20:18,814
Jati birth is a condition for Jaramarana.

126
00:20:19,182 --> 00:20:45,357
ah no how did this happen and to me where is my dynasty now my roots all shriveled my gorgeous head now bald and bent my leaves rotting eaten by worms such pain such agony jaramarana aging death lamentation despair

127
00:20:48,291 --> 00:20:57,961
Some friends from the Inside Meditation group in Dublin got together to illustrate the Sixth Sense Spears as their card for Bhante's book.

128
00:20:57,980 --> 00:21:04,567
Each card was made by a different person and, as we're not all great artists, don't expect consistency.

129
00:21:07,249 --> 00:21:10,531
The Buddha described the Sixth Sense Spears as the All.

130
00:21:11,393 --> 00:21:14,015
The Blessed One said, What is the All?

131
00:21:14,715 --> 00:21:16,897
Simply the I and Forms.

132
00:21:17,282 --> 00:21:28,436
ear and sounds, nose and aromas, tongue and flavors, body and sensations, intellect and ideas.

133
00:21:29,258 --> 00:21:31,701
This, monks, is called the All.

134
00:21:34,744 --> 00:21:37,387
Suppose the two oxen were joined by a yoke.

135
00:21:37,989 --> 00:21:44,156
If someone were to say, the ox on the left fetters the one on the right, would they be speaking rightly?

136
00:21:45,317 --> 00:21:46,159
No, my friend.

137
00:21:46,612 --> 00:22:15,505
neither ox fetters the other the yoke by which they are joined that is the fetter in the same way neither does the eye fetter visible forms nor do visible forms fetter the eye whatever desire and passion arises dependent on both that is the fetter in this illustration of the sense sphere of vision we have the eyes of wisdom

138
00:22:15,821 --> 00:22:42,723
then below in the lower realm you could say the eyes that have been blinded by what they desire the sense sphere of the ear and sound is illustrated around a poem by billy collins titled another reason why i don't keep a gun in the house with the buddha and kuan ying lending their compassion and wisdom to the initially fraught situation

139
00:22:44,324 --> 00:22:47,106
The neighbour's dog will not stop barking.

140
00:22:47,548 --> 00:22:52,973
He's barking the same high, rhythmic bark that he barks every time they leave the house.

141
00:22:53,775 --> 00:22:55,576
They must switch him on on their way out.

142
00:22:56,598 --> 00:22:59,962
The neighbour's dog will not stop barking.

143
00:23:00,623 --> 00:23:05,769
I close all the windows in the house and put on a Beethoven symphony full blast.

144
00:23:06,589 --> 00:23:10,134
But I can still hear him muffled under the music.

145
00:23:10,154 --> 00:23:12,998
Barking, barking, barking.

146
00:23:14,107 --> 00:23:22,756
And now I can see him sitting in the orchestra, his head raised confidently as if Beethoven had included a part for a barking dog.

147
00:23:23,777 --> 00:23:30,423
When the record finally ends, he's still barking, sitting there in the oboe section, barking.

148
00:23:31,403 --> 00:23:42,714
His eyes fixed on the conductor, who is entreating him with his baton, while the other musicians listen in respectful silence to the famous barking dog solo.

149
00:23:43,268 --> 00:23:48,955
that endless coda that first established Beethoven as an innovative genius.

150
00:23:52,280 --> 00:24:02,896
To illustrate the scent sphere of the nose and aromas, we track through a lifetime of smells from infancy to our teenage and adult years and eventually old age.

151
00:24:03,698 --> 00:24:10,307
Our path through life is marked by the desire and passion that arise for each aroma, fettering us.

152
00:24:11,088 --> 00:24:12,651
As we get older and wiser,

153
00:24:12,917 --> 00:24:19,105
we may respond with equanimity, but if we're not careful, we'll sink back into delusion.

154
00:24:22,950 --> 00:24:37,248
To illustrate the sense sphere of the tongue and taste, we have this meditating monk surrounded by sumptuous delicacies, which he is letting float on by, refusing to get himself tethered by desire and passion for food.

155
00:24:38,169 --> 00:24:42,654
He knows the tongue, he knows flavours, and he knows the fetter,

156
00:24:42,954 --> 00:24:45,898
arises dependent on both.

157
00:24:45,919 --> 00:24:56,994
And he also knows how an unarisen fetter can arise, how an arisen fetter can be removed and how to prevent fetters arising in the future.

158
00:25:00,859 --> 00:25:10,093
Remembering that emotional pain is felt in the body, the sense fear of the body and touch is illustrated around a poem by Khalil Gibran.

159
00:25:11,086 --> 00:25:15,070
Your pain is the breaking of the shell that encloses your understanding.

160
00:25:15,913 --> 00:25:22,340
Even as the stone of the fruit must break, that its heart may stand in the sun, so must you know pain.

161
00:25:23,403 --> 00:25:27,288
Could you keep your heart in wonder at the daily miracles of your life?

162
00:25:27,929 --> 00:25:30,752
Your pain would not seem less wondrous than your joy.

163
00:25:31,653 --> 00:25:38,763
And you would accept the seasons of your heart, even as you have always accepted the seasons that pass over your fields.

164
00:25:39,502 --> 00:25:43,429
And you would watch with serenity through the winters of your grief.

165
00:25:44,490 --> 00:25:46,653
Much of your pain is self-chosen.

166
00:25:47,193 --> 00:25:51,941
It is the bitter potion by which the physician within you heals your sick self.

167
00:25:53,462 --> 00:25:58,810
Therefore trust the physician and drink his remedy in silence and tranquility.

168
00:25:59,571 --> 00:26:05,400
For his hand, though heavy and hard, is guided by the tender hand of the unseen.

169
00:26:06,221 --> 00:26:08,565
And the cup he brings, though it burn your lips,

170
00:26:09,051 --> 00:26:15,501
has been fattened of the clay which the potter has moistened with his own sacred tears.

171
00:26:18,886 --> 00:26:29,523
The card illustrating the sphere of the mind and the thoughts, emotions, feelings and so on that it detects was inspired by something Bhante said to one of the group a few years ago.

172
00:26:30,766 --> 00:26:34,991
The sun always rises but you can never trust the mind.

173
00:26:36,810 --> 00:26:39,192
I'm always saying the wrong thing.

174
00:26:39,773 --> 00:26:40,634
I'm horrible.

175
00:26:41,255 --> 00:26:42,435
But he shouldn't have said that.

176
00:26:42,496 --> 00:26:43,477
It's all his fault.

177
00:26:44,218 --> 00:26:46,239
I wouldn't have said anything so insensitive.

178
00:26:46,480 --> 00:26:47,220
He's a brute.

179
00:26:48,340 --> 00:26:49,942
No one appreciates me.

180
00:26:51,523 --> 00:26:52,944
But I shouldn't have said that.

181
00:26:53,005 --> 00:26:55,207
I'm always saying the wrong thing.

182
00:26:55,567 --> 00:26:56,147
I'm horrible.

183
00:26:56,548 --> 00:26:57,108
I'm horrible.

184
00:26:57,449 --> 00:26:57,990
I'm horrible.

185
00:26:59,230 --> 00:27:01,633
I'm always saying the wrong thing.

186
00:27:01,653 --> 00:27:03,154
Oh.

187
00:27:03,994 --> 00:27:04,576
Thinking.

188
00:27:05,195 --> 00:27:05,957
Thinking.

189
00:27:08,317 --> 00:27:11,500
Thus we learn how to let go of existing fetters.

190
00:27:14,826 --> 00:27:18,431
The final card is our illustration of the end of suffering.

191
00:27:19,010 --> 00:27:22,977
The ox, our human nature, once tethered is now free.

192
00:27:23,597 --> 00:27:37,175
It no longer needs guidance from our Buddha nature, which rides fearlessly along with us, no longer looking ahead in anticipation of what's to come, but free to gaze serenely into nirvana where all things cease.

193
00:27:38,978 --> 00:27:48,279
Knowing how fetters arise, how to escape existing fetters, and how to prevent new fetters arising, one is free.

